 
//user macros slice 3 landed: `macro name(p: Expr, n: i32){...}` + `name!(...)`
//-- an `Expr` parameter is a syntax slot (each reference is replaced by a copy
//of the argument, the body is copied per call site), any other declared type is
//a value parameter (bound once, typed, at the top of the expansion). Statement
//+ expression position; looked up by bare name in this unit, then in the units
//it imports; the names the body declares are alpha-renamed per call site, so a
//body local can neither collide with nor capture a caller name.
//still open: token streams (resolver/macros.x stub), `use` aliases and scoped
//calls (`m::name!(...)`), and a body name that is never declared still resolves
//at the call site (definition-site resolution)

